findings.description:
Review-1 finding 1 has two parts:
- a root that apt cannot reinstall drops out silently (fixed);
- installed roots acl and python3 stay tied to the archive. Both verifiers said this second part contradicts ADR-0009 (B), which says a package the image already carries "is used as installed and not downloaded", and its tradeoff claim that (B) "ends the dependency on the archive and the runner image moving in step" (docs/DECISIONS.md:470, :472).
The disposition ("The residual ... is recorded as a limit in KI-0189; not fixed") and the review packet README:43 ("One limit is recorded rather than fixed") say this truthfully. But three status records say every surviving finding was corrected:
- KNOWN_ISSUES.md:77: "had every surviving finding corrected";
- PROJECT_STATUS.md:90: "had every surviving finding corrected";
- TEST_EVIDENCE.md:12734: "each is corrected".
The deviation from the accepted ADR's wording for the reinstalled roots is recorded only as a KI-0189 limit, not against ADR-0009. Behaviour fails closed, so this is a records-accuracy issue, not a safety issue.
